  "simulation_boundary": "All game/session/record paging, retranslation, save failure and delay states use deterministic page-local design fixtures. No network, real storage, native calls, production ports or service execution. Existing shared guided demo actions remain page-local simulations.",
  "fixture_boundary": "record -> session -> game. Existing source samples from LunaDesignData.games.lines; 57 sessions per game, three dense sessions over 50 lines, independent manual-input sessions, explicit no-history game, and a zero-record session. Fixed reference date 2026-10-31, Asia/Shanghai.",
  "state_boundary": "Page-local persistent history root survives parent full and private main renders, retaining draft focus and selection range. Filtering replaces the first 50; older-page loading appends within a frozen ID window. Independent record/session generation and request identities reject stale results. Errors preserve existing records, filters and selection; previous-scope records are explicitly labeled. Retry retains failed replace-versus-append semantics. Edits disable navigation/loading and save failures keep the draft. Locating the current record pins it by reordering the same frozen ID window before slicing the first page; the cursor remains aligned with consumed IDs.",
  "public_api": "window.LunaHistoryDesign: getState, setupScenario, setReviewState, chooseGame, chooseSession, loadMoreRecords, loadMoreSessions, retry, refreshRecords, locateCurrent, selectRecord, beginEdit, saveEdit, cancelEdit, settle; fixtures are design-only snapshots.",
  "review_states": [
    "default",
    "initial",
    "records-loading",
    "records-error",
    "records-end",
    "sessions-loading",
    "sessions-error",
    "sessions-empty",
    "empty",
    "long"
  ],
  "approval_boundary": "Pending user design review. Does not resolve approved-target closure gaps, replace confirmed sources/screenshots, grant independent state reference approval, or claim production/native/game/service/release acceptance."
